/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-436-1. **PUMPKIN Pi "checked transformations"** (RAW:271, 1132). The equivalence is checked. The transformation is explicitly *not*
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-437-   proven correct ("no need to formally prove the transformation correct", p7), its output is re-checked by Coq, and the decompiler
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-438-   "deliberately forfeits soundness" (p11). READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-439-2. **The quotient follow-up undersold** (RAW:1132). Its point is behaviour change and the "first ever internal proofs of correctness for proof
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-440-   repair" (p1), not only many-to-one representations. READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-441-3. **Ludics' daimon gap overstated** (RAW:402). Ludics already separates what interaction visits (incarnation, materiality, Def 5.1 p24) from
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-442-   daimon padding (daimon closure, Def 5.5 p26). The GPT presents the distinction as something "the language needs" that ludics lacks.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-443-   READ (incarnation); the Locus Solum winning-design point is INFERRED.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-444-4. **de Kleer attribution** (RAW:144). The resume/control-decision passage is real (printed p130), but "his proposed interface" is in de
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-445-   Kleer [8], not this paper. The GPT also omitted the ATMS's defining guarantee, labels "consistent, sound, complete and minimal" (printed
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-446-   ~p145), which is the part our design lacks. READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-447-5. **The TMS lineage**. Supports+blockers are Doyle's 1979 IN/OUT-list justifications, and nonmonotonic TMS = stable models is Elkan 1990.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-448-   The GPT cites only the ATMS (which, as a monotone system, has no OUT-lists) and cites stable models separately, so the identity
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-449-   "our judge's alternative labellings ARE stable models" never appears. READ-SCRY.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-450-6. **GKT 2007 cited for a design with negation** (RAW:115). GKT is RA+/positive Datalog only. Our blockers need Grädel–Tannen's
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-451-   N[X, X̄], which the GPT also cites, but it presents GKT as the core interpretation without the restriction. READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-452-7. **Demanded AI "with cyclic dependencies"** (RAW:546). The program's loops are cyclic; the DAIG is kept acyclic (p13). It is a nuance,
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-453-   not an error. READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-454-8. **Hazelnut Live's effect restriction understated** (RAW:1140). Purity is a *precondition* of the fill-and-resume theorem ("Languages with
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-455-   non-commutative effects do not enjoy this property", p22), not a remark about "speculative external effects". READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-456-9. **CakeML resource exhaustion** (RAW:1037). The paper says programs halt with OOM (specified behaviour). Only reclamation of dynamic code
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-457-   is open (p3). READ.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-458-10. **Stellar resolution scope** (RAW:404). The result is MLL only. The GPT did not state the restriction. READ.
