decisions/gates.md:432:## GATES-19 · The landing queue: behind-main is a judged merge, readiness order with an age bound, verdicts carried only under a byte-identical input key (2026-10-19/20, ROOT rulings; design docs/record/GATES-19-DESIGN.md)
decisions/gates.md:467:## GATES-20a · A run is selected by every binary it runs, not only its own: spawning rows, declared drives, and names in the static key (2026-10-20, ROOT ruling; found by GATES-8's traced read-sets)
decisions/gates.md:487:## GATES-20b · The landed copy: every path is merged from what the lander recorded, never taken from the working tree; a landing that would revert a recent commit is refused `stale path` unless named; a head lander is never charged for a tie (2026-10-21, ROOT rulings; HOSTING-13's hazard, LANG-21's finding)
decisions/gates.md:514:## GATES-20 · Traced read-sets select the runs and key the reuse; the judge's code is main's, the candidate supplies only its table (2026-10-20, landed 10-21 after GATES-20b; ROOT rulings F1/F2 and "the judge's CODE is main's"; design docs/record/GATES-20-DESIGN.md)
decisions/gates.md:580:## GATES-20d · A compile's reads are C, compared only against a compile; an escaped name invalidates the trace; an implied directory is not an extra (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; standing 145283a RED)
decisions/gates.md:608:## GATES-20e · A judge table is an input of every row it judges: a changed waste ceiling selects the row that measured it, standing-only included (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; PERF-4's fail-open at 41e041f)
decisions/gates.md:628:## GATES-20f · A dead lander's scratch is reaped at a later lander's start, by liveness only (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; PROTOCOL-21's 709572)
decisions/gates.md:642:## GATES-20b′ · A prior commit's change is contained when the copy holds it, whatever its context (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; PERF-6's false positive)
decisions/gates.md:654:## GATES-22 · The fast landing and the convergence: a landing is judged by what it reaches, the whole system every 3 h, a red names the commits it read (2026-10-21, Ember's ruling via ROOT)
decisions/gates.md:696:## GATES-20k · A failure of the tracer is not a verdict: UNREAD(tracer), re-run once, twice NOT JUDGED; a retry that passes is a counted flake (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; GATES-10 verified at source)
decisions/gates.md:706:## GATES-20j · A skipped cargo test is never ok: INCOMPLETE in pre-push, RED in standing; `cargo-untraced:` rows run without the tracer (2026-10-21, ROOT ruling; HOSTING-15's fence, built and planted by GATES-10)
decisions/gates.md:719:## GATES-20g · Rows run concurrently on free judge slots, each in its own scratch; GATES-20l · the convergence carries what the delta cannot reach, for at most a day (2026-10-21, Ember's question via ROOT; GATES-11 measured, GATES-12 built)
